  "description_html": "Comparison of skulls from 3 dfferent genera of <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tyrannosauridae\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tyrannosauridae\">tyrannosauridae</a> <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Dinosaurs\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dinosaurs\">dinosaurs</a>. The skulls of Tyrannosauridae are very caractheristic, with fused bones, special muscle attachment, and sharp teeth shaped like <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Banana\" title=\"Banana\">bananas</a>, and deeply rooted in the jaw. Many genera also show signs of <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Eye\" title=\"Eye\">eyes</a> faced forward, which may gave <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Binocular_vision&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Binocular vision (page does not exist)\">binocular vision</a>.\n<ul><li><b>1.</b> <i>Tarbosaurus bataar</i> (based on holotype PIN 551/1). Found in <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Mongolia\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mongolia\">Mongolia</a>, dated 74 - 65 million years old.\n<ul><li>Big skull with large air pockets to reduce the weight,<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and a brain only the volume of about 1, 85 - 1, 9 decilitres<sup id=\"cite_ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>Snout is narrower than in <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tyrannosaurus_rex\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tyrannosaurus rex\">Tyrannosaurus rex</a></i>, and the grade of forwardfacing of the eyes vary.<sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>2.</b> <i>Daspletosaurus torosus</i> (based on specimen FMNH PR308). Found in <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Alberta\" title=\"Alberta\">Alberta</a>, dated 75 million years old. Belived to be the ancestor of <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tyrannosaurus_rex\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tyrannosaurus rex\">Tyrannosaurus rex</a></i>.\n<ul><li>Small horns above the eyes.</li>\n<li>Eyes faced to the sides in some specimens (like FMNH PR308),<sup id=\"cite_ref-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> but some specimens may had eyes faced forward (MOR 590).<sup id=\"cite_ref-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>3.</b> <i>Gorgosaurus libratus</i> (based on TMP 91.36.500). Found in Alberta, dated 75 million years old.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>4.</b> <i>Bistahieversor</i> (based on the holotype NMMNH P-27469). Found in New Mexico, dated to about 74 million years old.</li>\n<li>Not a member of family Tyrannosauridae, but a more basal relative.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>5.</b> <i>Albertosaurus sarcophagus</i>. Found in Alberta, dated 75 million years old.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>6.</b> <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tyrannosaurus_rex\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tyrannosaurus rex\">Tyrannosaurus rex</a></i> (Based on specimen MOR 555, aka. \"Wankel rex\"). Found in <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Montana\" title=\"Montana\">Montana</a>, <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/South_Dakota\" title=\"South Dakota\">South Dakota</a>, <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/New_Mexico\" title=\"New Mexico\">New Mexico</a> and <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Utah\" title=\"Utah\">Utah</a>, dated 68-65 million years old.</li>\n<li>Skull was up to 5 feet long, and many specimens found have complete skulls, like \"Stan\" (BHI 3033), \"Sue\" (FMNH PR2081), and \"Harley\".<sup id=\"cite_ref-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>1. Massive skull without horns. The brain cavity had a size of almost a hole litre.<sup id=\"cite_ref-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>2. Eyes faced forward.</li></ul>\n<p>Binocular vision is also known in some specimens of the genera <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Albertosaurus\" title=\"Albertosaurus\">Albertosaurus</a></i> and <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Nanotyrannus&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Nanotyrannus (page does not exist)\">Nanotyrannus</a></i> ( the last is a possible synonym to <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tyrannosaurus\" title=\"Tyrannosaurus\">Tyrannosaurus</a></i> ). For example, <i>Albertosaurus</i> shows both forwardfaced eyes to some degree.<sup id=\"cite_ref-8\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> or faced to the sides.<sup id=\"cite_ref-9\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> <i>Nanotyrannus</i> also shows signs of binocular vision in the specimen \"Jane\".<sup id=\"cite_ref-10\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Referenses\">Referenses</h4></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.dinosaur-world.com/tyrannosaurs/tarbosaurus_bataar.htm\">http://www.dinosaur-world.com/tyrannosaurs/tarbosaurus_bataar.htm</a></i>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.nhm.uio.no/fagene/zoologi/forhistoriske-dyr/dinosaurer/tarbosaurus/english/videre03.htm\">http://www.nhm.uio.no/fagene/zoologi/forhistoriske-dyr/dinosaurer/tarbosaurus/english/videre03.htm</a></i>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.gondwanastudios.com/img/tarbosaur.jpg\">http://www.gondwanastudios.com/img/tarbosaur.jpg</a></i>, <i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.angelfire.com/mi/dinosaurs/images/casts/tarbo_skull_large_f.jpg\">http://www.angelfire.com/mi/dinosaurs/images/casts/tarbo_skull_large_f.jpg</a></i> and <i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.oucom.ohiou.edu/dbms-witmer/collections/Theropods/tarbosaurus.htm\">http://www.oucom.ohiou.edu/dbms-witmer/collections/Theropods/tarbosaurus.htm</a></i>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-4\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/astrangerinthealps/3984099880/sizes/l/\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/astrangerinthealps/3984099880/sizes/l/</a></i></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-5\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-5\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/mainman/2868974469/sizes/o/\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/mainman/2868974469/sizes/o/</a></i></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-6\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-6\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.fossils-as-art.com/images/trex-harley-skull.jpg\">http://www.fossils-as-art.com/images/trex-harley-skull.jpg</a></i></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-7\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-7\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.fieldmuseum.org/SUE/about_vital.asp\">http://www.fieldmuseum.org/SUE/about_vital.asp</a></i></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-8\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-8\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/_QC0xe56GvUo/SCbUA5nfKGI/AAAAAAAABF0/z__l3JaUvT8/s1600-h/IMG_0614.JPG\">http://3.bp.blogspot.com/_QC0xe56GvUo/SCbUA5nfKGI/AAAAAAAABF0/z__l3JaUvT8/s1600-h/IMG_0614.JPG</a></i></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-9\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-9\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/mujamed/3101708870/\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/mujamed/3101708870/</a></i></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-10\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-10\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><i><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/haikiba/2067321038/\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/haikiba/2067321038/</a></i></span>\n</li>\n</ol>",
